 {"id": "MON-GAP-031","type": "finding","lane": "monitoring","status": "pending","priority": "P1","complexity": 2,"source": "monitoring-foreman-2026-10-20-21-30-45","capability_tags": ["+monitoring","backup","disk-capacity","staging","sigkill"],"title": "MON-GAP-031 — a SIGKILLed backup-tiered.sh run strands ~84GiB of verify_/tmp_legacy_ staging on the root disk until the NEXT backup run fires (the EXIT trap cannot run on SIGKILL); this staging residue is the named churn behind karahermes DiskWillFillIn24h","reasoning": "WHY: the karahermes-mde-7840hs DiskWillFillIn24h alert (open row MON-MONITORING-EE32DFF5-20261020) is driven by churn on the root NVMe, and the single largest named contributor found this tick is backup-tiered.sh staging residue. EVIDENCE (2026-10-20 21:38-21:45 local, witness=local:df+sudo:find+fuser+pgrep): /var/tmp/hermes-backup-staging held 84.1GiB — verify_3778050.db 36,303,282,176B + verify_3778050.db-shm/-wal, tmp_legacy_3778050.db 36,303,282,176B, hermes-main/state.db.zst 12,234,546,651B (+4 small artifacts), hermes-foreman/state.db.zst 1,599,964,531B. The producing run opened .backup.lock at 12:10 and its last write was 13:33 (verify scratch of the same PID 3778050); state-backup.log shows its hermes-main tier uploaded to S3 at 12:58 and its hermes-foreman tier landed at 13:09 (S3+HDD+LOCAL-DIR), then silence — the run died mid-verify with no log line and no EXIT-trap cleanup. Liveness at probe time: flock -n on .backup.lock FREE (no active run), pgrep backup-tiered/backup-state empty, fuser empty on both 36GB files. By the script's own doctrine (backup-tiered.sh lines 101-103: everything already in STAGING is dead code by definition once the flock is held by a fresh run; lines 104-113 wipe on EXIT/INT/TERM and at run start) the residue was safe to reclaim — reclaimed this tick (df / 191,125,360KiB -> 299,562,740KiB free incl. a separate 24.3GiB stale-scratch sweep). ROOT CAUSE: the cleanup paths all require the run to still be alive; SIGKILL (or a host kill) skips the traps, and the next run's start-wipe is the only backstop — with runs landing ~every 6h+ a dead run can hold 80-84GiB on the ROOT disk for hours. Compounding: /var/tmp/hermes-backup-staging is the script's fast-disk default (line 51) and only falls back to /mnt/bulk when /var/tmp has <150GiB free (lines 80-87), so peak verify scratch (script comment: ~5x state.db size) deliberately lands on the root NVMe. FIX SHAPE: (a) attribute the kill for the 12:10-13:33 run (journalctl for OOM-kill / systemd kill / harness tool cap — the script comment at lines 45-49 documents the same verify step consuming a cron cap in an earlier incident); (b) make cleanup independent of the run's traps: a systemd-tmpfiles age rule or a small timer that clears $STAGING when .backup.lock is free (same dead-by-definition proof — never while a run holds the flock); (c) consider staging the verify_/tmp_legacy_ scratch on /mnt/bulk (sequential write, USB-tolerant) or bounding the verify step so a killed run cannot strand 2x36GB. CLOSE CRITERION: a controlled run killed mid-verify leaves <1GiB of staging residue within one sweeper period (proven by staging a real run + kill, then measuring the dir), AND the kill source of the 2026-10-20 run is named with journal evidence.","foreman_note": "ch:trace row=MON-GAP-031 spec=none wave=none:foreman-direct test=staging-census+df-before-after+flock-free+fuser-empty doc=~/.hermes/scripts/backup-tiered.sh:51,80-113 prompt=~/.hermes/skills/dev/coding-hermes-foreman-monitoring/SKILL.md evidence=staging-census-2026-10-20T2138Z+df-2138-2152Z-local witness=local:df+local:pgrep+local:fuser verdict=none:pending commit=pending memory=none:repo-local\n\nsupervisor 2026-10-21T09:15Z: REPRODUCED with 94GiB. The 2026-10-21 00:00:43 run was SIGKILLed at the 7200s cron cap (02:00:43) while still inside the LOCAL-DIR step — log shows '01:37:33 LOCAL-DIR: keep 12' as the last line; the same step needs 37min on a clean run (18:50:02 -> 19:27:04). Debris seen: verify_397573.db 36.8G + tmp_legacy_397573.db 36.8G + hermes-main 23G + hermes-foreman 2.1G. Supervisor reclaimed all 94GiB at 09:10Z: root / 92%->86% (154G->247G free). NOTE the two facts are linked: the alternating 00:00/12:00 failures ARE the debris source (signature verify_<pid>.db), and the debris makes the NEXT run start with 94G less headroom against a 150GiB STAGING_REQUIRED_KB preflight. Durable fix candidates: (a) clean stale /var/tmp/hermes-backup-staging verify_*/tmp_legacy_* at run START (not only the EXIT trap, which cannot fire on SIGKILL), (b) move LOCAL-DIR before the daily promotion so the starved step is the cheap one, or (c) raise cron.script_timeout_seconds above 7200 for this job. Primary layers are healthy throughout: S3 hourly hermes-main-20261021-000043 (01:11:32Z) and daily dump (01:26:10Z) both landed.","created_at": "2026-10-20T21:55:30Z","updated_at": "2026-10-21T09:12:52Z"}
